Subject: [PATCH] Reconcile the wiki with the generator-only refactor and the
 correct repo

The wiki was last restructured 2026-08-01 and predates the 2026-08-15
generator-only refactor (ADR 0013), which deleted the bespoke terraform
trees, the numbered workflows, and the Stage 13 dogfood. 30 of 61 pages
describe structures that no longer exist.

Repository identity and moved files (10 pages, 14 links):
- saulpatinojr/HCW-Plan_LZDeployment -> HybridCloudWorks/Template-LZDeployment
- USER-CHECKLIST.md -> docs/USER-CHECKLIST.md (moved 2026-08-07)
- PROD-TODO.md -> TODO.md (PROD-TODO was retired)

Home.md:
- Status block refreshed: v0.9.0 -> v0.11.0, and the blocker list now points
  at REVIEW.md/TODO.md rather than the retired PROD-TODO.md.
- A banner over the whole Source Material section stating that the wiki
  predates ADR 0013, naming what was deleted, and pointing at the
  authoritative in-repo sources. One banner on the index governs every page
  below it, rather than 30 duplicated per-page banners.
- Motion summary no longer says "fork".

Getting-Started.md (the live operator guidebook, most load-bearing page):
- The seven-move motion said "FORK: CBTS forks (or copies) this repo to the
  client". Two things were wrong. It is not necessarily a fork - a plain
  clone or a downloaded archive with no GitHub-side representation must work
  (decision 0004). And there is no third-party consultancy in the motion;
  that premise was corrected at decision 0010. The operator runs it on their
  own machine under their own gh/az sessions, which is exactly what makes
  tenant confirmation load-bearing.
- Both corrections are called out inline rather than silently rewritten, so
  a reader who remembers the old wording knows it changed and why.
- The accounts list no longer says "administer the client's fork".

Not done here: per-page banners on the remaining source-material pages. The
Home.md section banner covers them, and the separate 2026-08-06 patch adds
per-page HISTORICAL banners to 11 of them.
